{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794850228,"nonce":"dhXAFYqq7qP3WgQ0NfvV4H+Doew=","title":"The web page says \"done\" whatever the program's exit status was","message":"index.html sets the title to \"\u003cmodule\u003e — done\" when the program worker finishes, and \"trapped\" when it\ntrapped, but never says the exit status. A program whose event loop throws exits with status 1 and the\ntitle still says \"done\"; the status appears only as the line \"exited with 1, in 148ms\" in #out. A test\nrunner that waits for the title (hxn's `hxn check hl --wasm --browser`, hxn git-bug ded8361) therefore\npassed a failing program.\n\nThe page now also sets `window.ashOutcome = { status, trapped }` and the `data-ash-status` attribute of\nthe document element when the program exits or the page fails (status -1, with the reason in `trapped`,\nwhen it failed before the program had a status). The title is unchanged, so runners that match it still\nwork.","files":null}]}